{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Swift\/Never\/defaultPosition(_:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"defaultPosition","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"position","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint","text":"UnitPoint","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI9UnitPointV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Scene","text":"Scene","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI5SceneP","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"\n","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" that specifies where to place a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"newly opened window relative to the screen bounds.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"position"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Return Value","type":"heading","anchor":"return-value"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A scene that uses a default position for new windows.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The first time your app opens a window from a particular scene","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"declaration, the system places the window at the center of the screen by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default. For scene types that support multiple simultaneous windows, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system offsets each additional window by a small amount to avoid"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"completely obscuring existing windows."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can override the default placement of the first window by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"applying a scene modifier that indicates where to place the window"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"relative to the screen bounds. For example, you can request that the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system place a new window in the bottom trailing corner of the screen:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"code":["@main","struct MyApp: App {","    var body: some Scene {","        WindowGroup {","            ContentView()","        }","        .defaultPosition(.bottomTrailing)","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The system aligns the point in the window that corresponds to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"specified ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint"},{"text":" with the point in the screen that corresponds","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the same unit point.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You typically use one of the predefined unit points — like","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint\/bottomTrailing","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" in the above example — but","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"you can also use a custom unit point. For example, the following","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"modifier aligns the point that’s one quarter of the way from the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"leading edge of the window with the point that’s one quarter of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the way from the leading edge of the screen, while centering the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"window in the y-dimension:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"code":["WindowGroup {","    ContentView()","}",".defaultPosition(UnitPoint(x: 0.25, y: 0.5))"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The modifier affects any scene type that creates windows in macOS,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"namely:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Window"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DocumentGroup"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Settings"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The value that you provide acts only as an initial default. During state"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"restoration, the system restores the window to the position that it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"last occupied."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Swift","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Swift\/Never"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"Sets a default position for a window.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/openswiftui\/swift\/never\/defaultposition(_:)"]}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"metadata":{"extendedModule":"OpenSwiftUI","role":"symbol